The curve rows agree with, and extend, cador-curve-length-and-sampling.issue.

** 2.6 32-bit integers

| # | expression | AutoCAD-2022 | BricsCAD V25 = V26 | clautolisp (both dialects) |
|---+---+---+---+---|
| 21 | =(+ 2147483647 1)= | -2147483648 (wraps) | 2147483648 | error |
| 22 | =(* 65536 65536)= | 0 (wraps) | 4294967296 | error |
| 23 | =(- -2147483648 1)= | -2.14748e+09 REAL | -2147483649 | error |
| 24 | =(abs -2147483648)= | 2.14748e+09 REAL | 2147483648 | an integer TYPE cannot name |
| 505 | =(- 2147483648)= | -2.14748e+09 REAL | -2147483648 INT | -2.14748e+09 / -2147483648.0 |
| 506, 507 | =2147483648=, its TYPE | REAL | INT | REAL |
| 511 | =(type -2147483648)= | REAL (the reader overflows before negating) | INT | INT |
| 517, 519 | =(fix 2147483648.0)=, =(fix -2147483649.0)= | REAL | REAL (2147483648.0) | error |
| 522, 57 | =(atoi "2147483648")=, ="99999999999"= | 2147483647 (CLAMPED) | the 64-bit value | an integer TYPE cannot name |
| 525 | =(rem 2147483648 7)= | 2.0 | 2 | 2.0 |
| 528, 529 | =(lsh 1 31)=, =(lsh 1 32)= | -2147483648, 1 | same (32-bit) | error |
| 530 | =(~ 2147483647)= | -2147483648 | same | same |

BricsCAD integers are 64-bit, except lsh / ~ (32-bit) and fix (a REAL past
2^31). This extends numeric-edges-vendor-divergences.issue.

** 2.7 Characters outside the file encoding

| # | expression | AutoCAD-2022 | BricsCAD-V25 Windows | BricsCAD-V26 macOS |
|---+---+---+---+---|
| 102, 542 | =(chr 300)=, printed | "," (code 44 = 300 mod 256) | "I" (best fit) | "\U+012C" (an escape) |
| 544 | =(ascii (chr 300))= | 44 | 73 | 300 |
| 545 | =(vl-string->list (chr 8364))= | (172) | (128) | (8364) |
| 537 | write-line (chr 300), (open f "w"), read back | (44 10) | (73 10) | the 8 bytes \U+012C |
| 538 | write-line "a中b" | "a-b" | "a?b" | "a\U+4E2Db" |
| 540 | same with "w,ccs=UTF-8" | "," | C4 AC (UTF-8) | C4 AC (UTF-8) |

So no product signals. AutoCAD keeps the low byte of the code point,
BricsCAD V25 best-fits to the code page, and V26 writes an escape. clautolisp
signals: WRITE-LINE "the character with code 300 cannot be encoded", under
--dialect autocad. See encoding-replacement-character-option.issue.
(Case 539, ="utf8"= as the MODE, is a probe mistake: WCMATCH read "w,*" as
an alternation.)

** 2.8 Caveat: READ + EVAL versus loaded code

Cases 241 and 250 fail on AutoCAD only because the LAMBDA is created by EVAL
of a READ form. P1F shows the same message in LOADED code, for a
=(function (lambda ...))= value called as =(f)=. Plain =(lambda ...)= in a
loaded file worked in P1/P2. This is an AutoCAD interpreted-code
peculiarity, not yet characterised. Do not model it without a loaded-code
probe.

* 3. clautolisp against the vendors

Generated by gaps.py: results/clautolisp-vs-vendors.org. Cases where the
dialect's answer is not of the same KIND as its vendor's:

- --dialect autocad vs AutoCAD 2022: 106 cases
- --dialect bricscad vs BricsCAD V26: 115 cases

The main groups, each worth its own fix ticket:

1. Integer range (2.6): clautolisp signals where AutoCAD wraps / converts
   to a real / clamps and BricsCAD widens. Some results cannot even be given
   a TYPE (cases 24, 57, 522: "No AutoLISP runtime type designator is
   defined for 2147483648").
2. Silent nil / value answers modelled as errors: setvar out of range
   (339-344, the other way round: clautolisp ACCEPTS what both vendors
   refuse); DCL calls without an active dialog (473-483: nil on the
   vendors, error in clautolisp); entmod of an incomplete list (301-302);
   boundp of a non-symbol (213-214); strcat / getvar / vl-symbol-value nil
   under bricscad (95, 335, 217).
3. Values the vendors return and clautolisp refuses: (max) / (min) / (-) /
   (/) with no argument = 0 (30, 31, 46, 47), (/ 0) = 0 (49), inf.0 from
   exp / atof / read (17, 60, 133), (ascii "") = 0 (99).
4. Wrong value: (distance '(0 0) '(1 1 1)) is 1.73205 in clautolisp; both
   vendors take the 2D distance, 1.41421 (case 266).
5. Errors the vendors raise and clautolisp does not: (append '(1) 2) (159),
   (distance '(0 0) '(1)) (265), (entnext nil) (288), entmakex with a
   malformed group (295), (textbox nil) (281), tblsearch / tblnext of a bad
   table (322, 325), rtos / angtos mode 9 (62, 70).
6. LOAD with onfailure (456): clautolisp CALLS the onfailure symbol
   ("Undefined AutoLISP function PCAT-FAIL"). AutoCAD returns it; BricsCAD
   signals.
7. Encoding (2.7) and ERRNO (errno-setvar-accepted-by-vendors.issue).
8. Crashes (2.1) are not to be modelled as crashes. Under --dialect
   bricscad / autocad, signal a [vendor-crash] error with a message naming
   the vendor behaviour, so that tests written against clautolisp do not
   pass code that kills the CAD.

* 4. Already recorded elsewhere in clautolisp

A sweep on 2026-11-03 of the spec, the dialect-warnings document and the
issues found these already-measured divergences relevant to error
detection. They are not repeated in the catalogue:

- integers: numeric-edges-vendor-divergences.issue;
- comparison chains: comparison-operators-vendor-semantics.issue (= 78, 79 here);
- vl-exit-with-error / -value outside a VLX: vl-exit-outside-vlx-caught-diverges.issue;
- a nil catch-all message on AutoCAD: alfe-cad-nil-catch-all-message.issue;
- ERROR present on BricsCAD only, message: clautolisp-error-silent-under-autocad.issue
  (P12 and the catalogue both see the bare word "error" inside a command, on
  V25 and V26. pjb's REPL measurement recorded there gave the message.
  So it is context-dependent, or the records still disagree: re-measure
  at the BricsCAD command line);
- vl-catch-all-apply of an UNDEFINED function escapes on AutoCAD:
  autocad-runtime-vlax-sleep-and-rest.issue;
- curves: cador-curve-length-and-sampling.issue;
- entmake / entmod / xdata vetting: vendor-probe-autocad-bricscad-divergences.issue,
  drawing-data-structures-parity.issue (BricsCAD drops invalid xdata silently),
  xdroom-xdsize-not-implemented.issue, entmake-subclass-group-order.issue;
- setvar range and ERRNO: spec SETVAR table (BricsCAD wraps OSMODE to 16
  bits; the catalogue's 99999 is refused by both, see 339);
- open encoding argument: open-third-argument-dialect-divergence.issue,
  open-ccs-bom-bricscad-windows-divergence.issue;
- princ / prin1 without an argument, foreach without a body, setf,
  vl-bb-ref: SPEC and dialect-warnings.

* 5. To do

1. Model per dialect, with tests: the P6, P11, P12 and P1F rows of 1;
   2.2-2.4 (one ticket per family: lists, strings, curves, entities,
   command); load / arxload onfailure (both bricscad and the clautolisp
   bug of 3.6).
2. Fix the clautolisp-own gaps of 3 that are not dialect questions:
   integers that TYPE cannot name, LOAD onfailure called, setvar range
   accepted.
3. [vendor-crash] diagnostics for 2.1 (reverse of an improper list under
   bricscad; command-s refusing input under autocad).
4. Make probe-error-handler.lsp a regular probe suite, if a top-level
   runner can be added to the harness (it needs a script line per command,
   not a catch-all).
5. Spec: a "Normative Rules: failure reporting" note per family, citing
   these case numbers.

* 6. Not measured

- AutoCAD GUI (acad.exe): every row here is accoreconsole. vla-* there
  failed for lack of COM, not for the reasons the rows show.
- Errors inside DCL action_tile callbacks and inside reactor callbacks
  (both need an interactive session).
- The exact *error* message for ESC on BricsCAD V25 Windows.
- AutoCAD LISPSYS 1 / 2: the encoding rows were taken at the profile's
  default. Record its value on the next run.
